        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;10.1.1.11 (telnet 31102)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;name: capstone-02&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;open ports:23 21 1918&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;port 21:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;hint-02a.png&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;There is a webservice running the port that corrosponds with the RFC that coverns IPv4 Addressing.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;hint-002b.png&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;There is a PCAP saved in the share folder of this machine that you should look at&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;/usr/share/cctc/Flag-02f.txt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;/usr/share/cctc/&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;capstone-bpf.pcap&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#001DBC;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-4">
          <mxGeometry x="33.98164990904912" y="-0.6440677966101696" width="285.44585923601255" height="211.5084745762712" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-7" value="" style="group;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" connectable="0" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1860" y="3680" width="310" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-8" value="" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;sketch=0;aspect=fixed;html=1;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;align=center;outlineConnect=0;shape=mxgraph.citrix.desktop;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-7">
          <mxGeometry width="19.96678486997636" height="21.98581560283688" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;10.1.1.25 ()&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;name:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;open ports:21 4969 791&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;hint-03a: There is a webservice running on the port that corresponds with the RFC that governs IPv4 Header Structure.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;hint-03b.png: There is another hint in the student home drive. There is no SSH access to this system so try using FTP wih your student credentials&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;hint-03c.png: There is a listening TCP port on this system that waiting for connections. Build a Python3 TCP Stream sender and send it thru your tunnel to say Hi. Send your message as a bytes-like object and decode the response to/from UTF-8 to get the double encoded message. You can use CyberChef to help you decode the message to human readable.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#001DBC;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-7">
          <mxGeometry x="32.97872340425532" y="0.5544" width="277.02127659574467" height="329.4456" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-10" value="" style="group;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" connectable="0" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2200" y="3680" width="310" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-11" value="" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;sketch=0;aspect=fixed;html=1;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;align=center;outlineConnect=0;shape=mxgraph.citrix.desktop;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-10">
          <mxGeometry width="19.96678486997636" height="21.98581560283688" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;10.1.1.30 ()&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;name:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;open ports:80&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;hint-01a.png: This system seem to be a pivot for the Network Fundamentals and Programming sections.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#001DBC;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-10">
          <mxGeometry x="32.97872340425532" y="0.42" width="277.02127659574467" height="249.58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-13" value="" style="group;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" connectable="0" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2550" y="3680" width="470" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-14" value="" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;sketch=0;aspect=fixed;html=1;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;align=center;outlineConnect=0;shape=mxgraph.citrix.desktop;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-13">
          <mxGeometry width="19.966784869976355" height="21.985815602836873" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;10.1.1.33 (telnet 31104)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;name:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;open ports:23 21 80&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;hint-04a.png: There is another box (Capstone-05) on a different network (that only this system can see) trying to attack this box, on one of the port(s) associated with the W32/Blaster Worm. Use a sniffing tool to try to find the message it is trying to send.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;hint-04b.png: RIPv2 seems 10 be running on the 10.1.1.0/25 network. Try to sniff out the traffic to find out what networks its advertising in its updates. What you find will be the IP address of the next environment pivot to access from your INTERNET_HOST.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;use internal recon techniques for this&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot; color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;sudo tcpdump -i eth0 &#39;udp port 520 and net 10.1.1.0/25&#39; -XXn&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#001DBC;" vertex="1" parent="FMMKwEJgUoLVOogY_UPH-13">
